# OS artifacts
.DS_Store
*.swp
*~

# Sensitive files
*.env
.env.*
credentials*.json
*.key
*.pem

# IDE
.idea/
.vscode/

# Local-only Claude Code settings (operator overrides, not shared)
.claude/settings.local.json

# Isolated git worktrees created by EnterWorktree (checkouts, never repo content)
.claude/worktrees/

# Python
__pycache__/
*.pyc

# Ephemeral audit working notes (subagent-contract discipline lives in CLAUDE.md, not as a deny rule)
audits/working/

# Ephemeral session scratchpads (/save-session outputs, implementation plans — lasting content graduates to session-notes or decisions.md)
logs/scratchpads/

# Concurrent-session detection marker written by /prime, read by /session-start Step 0.5
logs/.prime-mtime

# Per-session identity marker written by /prime (Phase 1 of TOCTOU-mitigation rollout per logs/improvement-log.md TOCTOU entry)
logs/.session-marker
# Per-session-id identity oracle (Option 2′, keyed by CLAUDE_CODE_SESSION_ID — un-clobberable by a concurrent /prime; see docs/session-marker.md)
logs/.session-marker-*

# Work Loop v2 per-checkout ownership declaration (R2, "the checkout declares its writer"): one task
# id + claim date, written by whoever creates the task's state file, cleared at closure. It MUST stay
# checkout-local — a committed copy would replicate across worktrees on merge and then declare every
# checkout the owner, which is the exact failure the declaration exists to refuse. Read/written by
# logs/scripts/work-loop-owner.sh; see docs/parallel-sessions-playbook.md § 4.
logs/work-loop/.owner

# Promotion mutex held by logs/scripts/promote-findings.sh for the length of one sweep. Removed by
# the script's own EXIT trap; ignored here so a crashed run's residue can never be committed.
logs/.promote.lock/

# Derived semantic-search index built by logs/scripts/memory-search.py (/memory-search command) —
# regenerable at any time via `/memory-search reindex`, never committed
logs/.memory-index/

# Archived inbox briefs (Layer C settings.json also denies Read on this path)
inbox/archive/

# Top-level archive directory only (anchored 2026-07-03 — the unanchored form silently ignored
# nested archive dirs, notably logs/missions/archive/, forcing `git add -f` on mission-close
# records; Layer C settings.json also denies Read on this top-level path)
/archive/

# Context-engine runtime output (packs are session artifacts; treated as untracked per operator policy)
output/

# Codex CLI harness mirror — operator experiment, NOT a maintained artifact (operator call, 2026-07-13 S12).
# It appeared untracked on 2026-07-13 as a full parallel port of the harness (~42 agents, 19 hooks, its own
# check-foreign-staging.sh) and was NOT gitignored, so any broad `git add` would have swept ~60 files into
# the repo. It also carries its own copy of the /lean-repo Q3 orphan lens, which is NOT kept in sync with
# the canonical fix (id-55) — a third copy nobody maintains is exactly the drift this repo keeps paying for.
# Ignored so it cannot be committed by accident. If Codex is ever adopted for real, the decision to track
# and sync this mirror is a deliberate one to make — not an outcome of a wildcard staging command.
#
# THREE FILES ARE NOW DELIBERATELY TRACKED (operator choice (a), 2026-08-08, Work Loop v2 slice S6).
# This is the deliberate decision the note above reserves, and it is narrowed to three named paths —
# it does NOT adopt or maintain the rest of the mirror. S6's post-compaction reorientation lives in
# these files, so leaving them untracked meant `git clean -x` could delete the slice silently and no
# commit could revert it. The remaining ~60 `.codex/` files stay ignored and unmaintained.
#
# Same ladder reason as the `.agents/` block below: git does not descend into an excluded directory,
# so `.codex/` had to become `.codex/*` before any negation inside it could be evaluated. `AGENTS.md`
# stays ignored at every depth; only the repository-root one is re-included, via the leading slash.
# Verified with `git check-ignore -v` after the edit.
.codex/*
!.codex/hooks.json
!.codex/hooks/
.codex/hooks/*
!.codex/hooks/work-loop-reorient.sh
AGENTS.md
!/AGENTS.md

# `.agents/` stays ignored EXCEPT the skills deliberately adopted (operator call, 2026-07-28 S3;
# extended to work-loop-v2, 2026-08-01 S6, and handoff-thread, 2026-08-07). This is the "deliberate
# decision to track" the note above reserves — narrowed to named subtrees, not an adoption of the
# mirror. The four `source-command-*` skills and the `wl2-probe` throwaway remain ignored and
# unmaintained; the Codex mirror does too, apart from the three S6 files named in the block above.
#
# The 2026-07-28 S3 entry `!.agents/skills/work-loop/` was removed on 2026-08-11 when the Work Loop
# v1 Codex controller skill was retired (Axcíon Harness v0.2 Phase 0). Nothing re-includes that path
# now, which is intended: v1 must not return to a fresh clone.
#
# Why a ladder and not one `!.agents/skills/work-loop-v2/`: git does not descend into an excluded
# directory, so a negation for a path inside `.agents/` never gets evaluated. Each level must be
# re-included before the next can be excluded. Verified with `git check-ignore -v` after the edit.
#
# Each adopted skill needs its OWN re-include line — a negation for one skill does not cover a
# sibling. Without one, a new resource works on this machine and does not exist in a fresh clone,
# silently (Work Loop v2 slice plan, "Two obligations that are not behaviours", item 1).
.agents/*
!.agents/skills/
.agents/skills/*
!.agents/skills/work-loop-v2/
!.agents/skills/handoff-thread/
!.agents/skills/reorient/
!.agents/skills/diagnose-and-fix/
